sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 4 of the command development pipeline (docs/reference/pipeline/4-pr-and-ci.mmd, "Review the PR head": the verdict is posted as a PR comment by the App). It follows tasks.pr_ready: the Gateway admits and names the vault key, the step mints its token, and Swamp calls GitHub.
  %% status: migrated
  %% kind: tasks.pr_comment
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  Note over GW: Admit the comment<br/>head · body · key name
  %%> Who calls it:
  %%> - the gate check `tasks:pr-gate`, once for each review round, after the reviewer turn ended; there is no command, route or MCP tool
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the group is an open external group with a published PR that is open, and the PR head is exactly the head of the round
  %%> - no other task runs on the group; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - builds the body from the verdict and the findings of the round
  %%> - names the vault key `pr-comment-write-<uuid>` for the write token; it mints no token
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-pr-comment
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); no Node is a target
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the repository, PR number, expected head and the comment body
  %%> - the vault key name of the token, never the token
  SW->>GW: Mint the token<br/>operation:direct:github-token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the first step posts the run id to the Gateway; the Gateway checks the Operation, the run and the repository, mints a token with only `pull_requests: write`, and writes it to the vault key that admission named
  %%> Why here and not at admission:
  %%> - an installation token lives one hour; the token is minted when the step that uses it runs
  %%> - no task VM holds a GitHub credential
  SW->>GH: Read the PR
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `gh api` read of the state and the head SHA
  Note over SW: Check the PR head
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a head other than the admitted one, or a PR that is no longer open, with `tasks_pr.head_moved`; nothing is posted
  SW->>GH: Post the comment
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - posts the body as a comment on the PR with the App token, passed by vault key name, so Nick can read the verdict on the PR
  SW->>GH: Revoke the token
  %%> When:
  %%> - always, on success and failure; best effort because the token expires within one hour
  Note over SW: Remove CLI config
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the private GitHub CLI configuration directory of this run
  Note over SW: Confirm the comment step
  alt posted
    GH-->>SW: Comment id
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the id of the new comment
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · comment id
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the result<br/>task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task succeeds with the comment id; the gate check goes on to the merge step or the fix
  else refused or failed
    GH--xSW: head moved or refused
    %%> When:
    %%> - the head moved or GitHub refused the comment
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, such as `tasks_pr.head_moved`
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>PR kept as it is
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task fails and the PR stays as it is; the gate check does not post the same comment again, because the admission is keyed by group and head
  end
